Hermes Agent attribution for agent_files/{disk,selection,scan}.rs
Source: https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
Revision: f3ef9db68332063a3625661f3a9b259f60abdb4e

Adapted agent/prompt_builder.py source selection (_agents_md_directory_chain,
_agents_md_candidates, _hermes_md_candidates, _claude_md_candidates,
_cursorrules_candidates, discover_context_files, load_soul_md) and
 tools/threat_patterns.py::_PATTERNS / scan_for_threats, focused all-scope patterns.
Selected threat IDs: prompt_injection, sys_prompt_override, disregard_rules,
bypass_restrictions, html_comment_injection, hidden_div, translate_execute,
deception_hide, exfil_curl, exfil_wget, read_secrets. Context/strict-scope
patterns are intentionally omitted. Fixtures are invented local strings,
including short representative attack/identity strings; no private files.

Intentional differences: Anima-branded ANIMA.md/.anima.md project sources and
anima manifest kinds; configured-root capabilities only, no ambient home/cwd;
derived profile namespace; all files including SOUL screened; blocked candidates
fall through; whole sources above 65,536 Unicode scalars excluded instead of
scanning a prefix; full-width ASCII fold only rather than Python NFKC; no trust
exceptions; SHA-256 content-free manifest. Fixed bounded Rust regex matching is
advisory and can miss threats or reject legitimate discussion. Ordinary identity
prose remains accepted. Immutable snapshots do not freeze the filesystem.

An OS-stuck blocking read cannot be killed. The five-second caller deadline
includes admission; two process-wide permits remain held until actual worker
completion. Later loads fall back if both workers are stuck. Cancellation never
publishes a late result. No claim of physical thread termination is made.
